# The Thor's two touchscreens (edt-ft5x06, named by their dts label)
#  - touchscreens only: their BTN_TOUCH otherwise makes them look like keyboards too, and the
#    wlroots seat in gamescope then took one for the keyboard (ROCKNIX 61-thor-ft5x06.hwdb)
#  - each mapped to its own screen in the desktop (KWin reads WL_OUTPUT). The top panel is on
#    DSI1 and the bottom one on DSI0: DSI-2 and DSI-1, as msm registers DSI0 first.
#  - both back in their panels' own (portrait) orientation, as the Portal's touchscreen reports:
#    the Thor's dts swaps and inverts the axes (touchscreen-swapped-x-y, -inverted-x), and
#    gamescope and KWin then rotated them a second time, with the screen. The matrix undoes it
#    (x = 1 - y, y = x); ROCKNIX's Thor quirk uses the same one. In Game Mode, gamescope passes
#    the bottom one's touches, in this orientation, to the bottom screen's gamescope.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="*_touchscreen", \
  ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}="0", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN}="1", \
  ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="0 -1 1 1 0 0"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="top_touchscreen", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="DSI-2"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="bottom_touchscreen", ENV{WL_OUTPUT}="DSI-1"
